Falsifies `driver_process_contract::non_volatile_memory_express::proofs::the_spawn_handoff_round_trips`.

The defect: `Handoff::pack` shifts `blocks_per` by 17 where `unpack` reads from bit 16. The data
plane then addresses twice the LBA it was told, and nothing between the two halves notices.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(Handoff::unpack(h.pack()), Some(h))`.

diff --git a/crates/driver_process_contract/src/non_volatile_memory_express.rs b/crates/driver_process_contract/src/non_volatile_memory_express.rs
--- a/crates/driver_process_contract/src/non_volatile_memory_express.rs
+++ b/crates/driver_process_contract/src/non_volatile_memory_express.rs
@@ -137,3 +137,3 @@ impl Handoff {
         [
-            (self.dstrd as u64) << 32 | (self.blocks_per as u64) << 16 | self.entries as u64,
+            (self.dstrd as u64) << 32 | (self.blocks_per as u64) << 17 | self.entries as u64,
             self.data_plane_phys,
